<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 June, from 1190 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1190">1190 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">836 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick Barbarossa drowns on the Third Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> drowned in the Saleph river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> while leading his army to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>. Much of the German crusading force broke up after his death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1225">1225 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">801 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Honorius III approves a Dominican mission to Morocco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the bull Vineae Domini custodes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a> approved a mission to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, then part of the Almohad empire, asked for by the friars Dominic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segovia">Segovia</a> and Martin. Its call to convert Muslims broke with earlier papal policy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1329">1329 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">697 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ottomans defeat a Byzantine army at Pelekanon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Ottoman army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orhan">Orhan</a> I defeated a Byzantine expeditionary force under Andronikos III at the Battle of Pelekanon. No further attempt was made to relieve the cities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> under Ottoman siege, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a> fell in 1331.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-ottoman-wars">Byzantine–Ottoman wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1422">1422 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">604 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sultan Murad II lays siege to Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> laid siege to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, the Byzantine capital, after Emperor Manuel II had tried to interfere in the Ottoman succession following Mehmed I's death. The siege failed; the city fell to Murad's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> in 1453.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1692">1692 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">334 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bridget Bishop is hanged in the Salem witch trials</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bridget <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> was the first person executed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salem-witch-trials">Salem witch trials</a>. By September eighteen more had been hanged, and one man had been pressed to death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">National Museum of Natural History is founded in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Convention reorganised the royal botanical garden as the Muséum national d'histoire naturelle. Scientists there, including Lamarck and Cuvier, transformed biology and palaeontology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">SS troops massacre the village of Oradour-sur-Glane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waffen-ss">Waffen-SS</a> unit killed 643 people in the French village, shooting the men and burning women and children in the church. The ruins are preserved as a memorial.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Six-Day War ends in a ceasefire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fighting ended with Israel holding Sinai, Gaza, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>, East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a>. The status of these territories has remained central to the conflict ever since.</p></div></li></ol>
